# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# .gitignore does NOT apply here. Anything not excluded below is uploaded to
# the daemon and can be captured by a careless COPY — and once it is baked
# into a published layer, deleting the file in a later layer does not remove
# it. A published image carrying a credential cannot be un-published.
#
# The entries in the first block are the reason this file exists. Do not
# remove them, and add any new secret location here at the same time as you
# create it. The image workflow also asserts their absence inside the built
# image, so a mistake here fails the build rather than shipping.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets: never in an image ----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
src/main/resources/keys/
secrets/

# --- version control and tooling ---------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# --- build output: the image builds its own ----------------------------------
# Copying a host-built target/ in would shadow the one produced inside the
# build stage, so the image could ship a jar compiled from different sources
# than the ones in the context.
target/
build/
out/
bin/

# --- not part of the runtime image -------------------------------------------
docs/
*.md
docker-compose.yml
compose*.yml
render.yaml

# --- editor leftovers and stray archives -------------------------------------
*~
*.orig
*.rej
*.zip
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
